1	commit 88ad45f84ba24df5efcbae73da09c653c7cfee16
2	Author: Sofiane Bebert <sofiane@bebert.co>
3	Date:   Sat Nov 14 23:36:34 2026 +0000
4	
5	    refactor(shell): hold one GmailCore in AppState and delete the Backend enum
6	    
7	    Backend::{Gmail, Synthetic} wrapped the same GmailCore in both arms, and
8	    its ~290-line forwarding impl did the same thing in every arm. AppState
9	    now holds the GmailCore (and its GmailUnsubscribe guard) directly and
10	    commands call it; run_blocking takes the core. The two renamed calls are
11	    core.enable_mutations / core.cancel_mutation_upgrade. The one piece of
12	    Backend logic, the reply-context re-check, becomes a free function in
13	    the shell until it moves to mail-core in the next commit. Nothing asks
14	    which session kind is open any more; setup and tests read it from the
15	    core's reported mode.
16	    
17	    No behaviour, IPC, DTO or generated-type change. Native tests: 18 -> 18;
18	    tests edited only for the Backend -> GmailCore rename.
19	    
20	    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
21	    Entire-Checkpoint: 01M7E6PZXH45YAVWERXYHCRP17
