commit 8e1a760e9bc162706e73e5e13e22d504447125bd
Author: Sofiane Bebert <sofiane@bebert.co>
Date:   Sat Nov 14 23:40:31 2026 +0000

    refactor: move account-scoped draft logic from the shell into mail-core

    active_account, require_draft_account, validate_reply_conversation, the
    reply-context re-check and the session-epoch lifecycle that serialises
    draft operations against connect/disconnect were mail rules living in
    src-tauri. They are now mail_core::drafts::DraftService (plus
    GmailCore::active_account), and the draft and account-session commands
    are one-line delegations. The create-draft flow, its lock order, the
    epoch check and the order of the epoch advance relative to
    connect/disconnect are copied unchanged. Lock-poison failures are now
    logged by mail-core's storage_log (same cause tag, target
    mail_core::storage, which the shell logger already admits).

    Core tests added (12): DraftService against the synthetic account and a
    signed-out Gmail core (every operation, foreign refs, idempotent create,
    reply sources, each validate_reply_conversation rejection, lifecycle
    rejection in a synthetic session) and the epoch rules (connect leaves it
    alone on failure, disconnect advances it first). The shell's draft test
    keeps its assertions; only imports and the active_account call changed.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Entire-Checkpoint: 01M7E6Y6HPYV1KA546GB44KDHC

