Date:   Sat Nov 14 23:42:33 2026 +0000

    refactor: move attachment transfer admission and cancellation into mail-core

    AttachmentTransfers (one transfer at a time, a bounded memory of cancelled
    request ids so an early cancel wins, request-id validation) decided mail
    download behaviour inside the shell, behind an Arc<Mutex> the commands
    locked by hand. It is now mail_core::attachments::AttachmentTransfers,
    cloneable and internally synchronised, with begin / cancel / finish; the
    save and cancel commands only translate IPC.

    The original unit test moves verbatim next to the state it inspects
    (exact 64-entry bound). The shell test of the same name stays and asserts
    the same behaviour through the public API (the bound is observed as r36
    refused, r35 admitted). Four more core tests cover the shared registry,
    id validation, memory eviction and a poisoned lock.

